  {
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "Does this provide an indication of how to do what you want:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom numba import cuda, types\r\nfrom numba.core.extending import overload\r\nimport numpy as np\r\n\r\n\r\ndef grid_position_like(index):\r\n    pass\r\n\r\n\r\n@overload(grid_position_like)\r\ndef grid_position_like_ol(index):\r\n    if index == types.int16:\r\n        def grid_position_like(index):\r\n            print(\"int16 variant\")\r\n            i_x, i_y = cuda.grid(2)\r\n            return (np.int16(i_x), np.int16(i_y))\r\n    elif index == types.int32:\r\n        def grid_position_like(index):\r\n            print(\"int32 variant\")\r\n            i_x, i_y = cuda.grid(2)\r\n            return (np.int32(i_x), np.int32(i_y))\r\n    elif index == types.int64:\r\n        def grid_position_like(index):\r\n            print(\"int64 variant\")\r\n            i_x, i_y = cuda.grid(2)\r\n            return (np.int64(i_x), np.int64(i_y))\r\n    else:\r\n        return None\r\n\r\n    return grid_position_like\r\n\r\n\r\n@cuda.jit\r\ndef f():\r\n    grid_position_like(np.int16(1))\r\n    grid_position_like(np.int32(1))\r\n    grid_position_like(np.int64(1))\r\n\r\n\r\nf[1, 1]()\r\ncuda.synchronize()\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhich prints:\r\n\r\n```\r\nint16 variant\r\nint32 variant\r\nint64 variant\r\n```\r\n\r\n(obviously not very efficient to print on CUDA, but hopefully indicates the distinct variants being compiled / called).",
