    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "> Yes - the generic version is good!\r\n> \r\n> ... are you saying it should already work? :) That's great!\r\n\r\nI was working with Numba `main`, which is pretty much exactly the same as the 0.57 RC at the moment. I'm not sure whether it'll work with 0.56.4 (I'd expect so, but it was so long ago that I've forgotten if something else went into 0.57 that enables it).\r\n\r\n> (NB - Apropos type comparisons (`isinstance(index, types.NumberClass)` etc) - I think the problem I had is that I like to be able to run using CUDASIM sometimes, and I think they may break in that case. Of course I can patch but as this goes in a library which is used by a few other repos it gets a bit messy. Perhaps the solution is simply to check CUDASIM in the overload function.)\r\n\r\nIf you replace the dummy `pass` in `grid_position_like` with an actual implementation, does that work under cudasim? Something like:\r\n\r\n```python\r\ndef grid_position_like(index):\r\n    i, j = cuda.grid(2)\r\n    return index(i), index(j)\r\n```\r\n\r\n(I have not tried the above, but only attempted to illustrate the idea).",
